<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>Known issues for Windows Server and/or Console upgrades - Trend Micro Endpoint Security Platform version 8.1.634.0</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[
<TABLE><TBODY><TR><TD><P><STRONG>Version&nbsp;8.1.634.0 of Trend Micro Endpoint Security Platform is now available!</STRONG></P> <P>The latest version of Trend Micro Endpoint Security Platform provides several enhancements and fixes. Click on the link below for more information on changes in Trend Micro Endpoint Security Platform 8.1.</P> <P>Windows Installer 3.1 or greater must be installed to perform this upgrade. Use the action below to install Windows Installer 3.1. Once this is complete, you can use <?Relevance link of fixlet whose (name of it contains "Updated Windows Server and/or Console - Trend Micro Endpoint Security Platform version 8.1.634.0") of site of current fixlet?>to upgrade Trend Micro Endpoint Security Platform Servers and Consoles to version 8.1.634.0.</P> <P><STRONG>Note:</STRONG> Affected computers may report back as 'Pending Restart' once the patch has run successfully, but the vulnerability will not be closed until the affected computer is restarted.</P> <P>If you have any issues during the upgrade, you may want to review the manual upgrade instructions below to help resolve the issues.</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>
]]></Description>
    <Relevance>name of operating system as lowercase starts with &quot;win&quot;</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[((it = "Win7" OR it = "Win2008R2" OR it = "Win2008" OR it = "WinVista") of name of it OR ((name of it = "Win2003" AND service pack major version of it >= 1) OR ((it = "WinXP" OR it = "WinXP-2003") of name of it AND service pack major version of it >= 2))) of operating system]]></Relevance>
    <Relevance>if (exists key &quot;HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\BigFix\Brand&quot; whose (exists value &quot;value&quot; of it) of registry) then (value &quot;value&quot; of key &quot;HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\BigFix\Brand&quot; of registry as string = &quot;Trend&quot;) else (&quot;Trend&quot;=&quot;BigFix&quot;)</Relevance>
    <Relevance>evaluation of client license = false</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[(exists service "BESRootServer" AND exists key "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\BigFix\Enterprise Server" whose (exists ((value "Version" of it) as string as version) whose (it < "8.1.634.0" AND it >= "7.0.1")) of registry) OR (exists regapp "BESConsole.exe" whose (version of it < "8.1.634.0" AND version of it >= "6"))]]></Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[not (exists file "msiexec.exe" whose (version of it >= "3.1") of system folder)]]></Relevance>
    <Category>Upgrade</Category>
    <Source>IBM</Source>
    <SourceID>&lt;Unspecified&gt;</SourceID>
    <SourceReleaseDate>2012-01-31</SourceReleaseDate>
    <SourceSeverity>Critical</SourceSeverity>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-first-propagation</Name>
      <Value>Tue, 31 Jan 2012 21:19:33 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Mon, 30 Jul 2012 22:05:05 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-domain-attributes</Name>
      <Value>BES Deploy Server Console</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to install Windows Installer 3.1 on relevant computers.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">prefetch WindowsKBforServer.exe sha1:8318455b36ba0a748307459279d46f2f4cdb5a0e size:2585872 http://download.microsoft.com/download/1/4/7/147ded26-931c-4daf-9095-ec7baf996f46/WindowsInstaller-KB893803-v2-x86.exe
delete __Local/Get/WindowsKBforServer.exe
move __Download/WindowsKBforServer.exe __Local/Get/WindowsKBforServer.exe
wait __Local/Get/WindowsKBforServer.exe /passive /quiet /norestart
delete __Local/Get/WindowsKBforServer.exe
action may require restart</ActionScript>
    </DefaultAction>
    <Action ID="Action289">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> for manual upgrade instructions.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="text/x-uri">http://support.bigfix.com/bes/install/upgradebes.html</ActionScript>
    </Action>
    <Action ID="Action290">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to see the new features in Trend Micro Endpoint Security Platform 8.1.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="text/x-uri">http://support.bigfix.com/bes/changes/changes-8.1.html</ActionScript>
    </Action>
    <Action ID="Action291">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to view the Microsoft Windows Installer 3.1 information page.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="text/x-uri">http://support.microsoft.com/?id=893803</ActionScript>
    </Action>
  </Fixlet>
</BES>
